// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO20 - dedicated power-enable pin for the
// onboard I2C peripherals (NEOPIXEL_I2C_POWER, vendor comment "I2C power
// pin"), not general-purpose. GPIO9 (NeoPixel data, PIN_NEOPIXEL) stays
// available.
// pfodWeb NOTE (button/LED tagging pass): GPIO15 (LED_BUILTIN) confirmed
// onboard red status LED, active-high (Adafruit's own board-specific
// Arduino Blink tutorial: "digitalWrite(led, HIGH); // turn the LED on"),
// tagged led_high. GPIO9 (PIN_NEOPIXEL) confirmed onboard NeoPixel, tagged
// led_neopixel - vendor docs also state GPIO9 is physically shared with
// the onboard BOOT button (input w/ pullup), so only one of the two
// functions can be used at a time; no separate "button" tag was applied
// since this file has no BUTTON symbol and PIN_NEOPIXEL is the documented
// use of this pin. GPIO20 exclusion (above) re-confirmed: vendor guide
// states the NEOPIXEL_I2C_POWER gate is driven automatically by the
// Arduino core, not by user sketch code. See boardsDetails notes.txt for
// full sourcing.
